Kind: ablation
Issue: #417
Takes out: the reach device_dma_alloc reads from the device's claim: every buffer is placed as for a device that reaches everything.  On entry 70 edu's buffer within its declared 28 bits is given an IOVA from 4 GiB, and libdriver must say the kernel placed it past the reach it was told.
Run: --iommu intel --edu --entry 70 600 -smp 4
Expect: edu_probe@[0-9a-f]{2}:[0-9a-f]{2}\.[0-7]: the kernel placed a DMA buffer at device address 0x[0-9a-f]+, past the 0xfffffff it was told the device reaches

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/device/device_master.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/device/device_master.c
index 0cfb77ec..6f1ea7d8 100644
